# oracle-inputs: w12tip4p_long_water.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 3.1e-13, atoms 5.3e-12.
# oracle: pair_style hybrid/overlay of lj/cut/tip4p/long (O-O, O-H LJ and M-site Coulomb) and lj/cut (H-H LJ with eps 0.1 sigma 2.0, which is large enough to load the virial of the fdotr sub-style), 27 rigid TIP4P/2005 waters, pppm/tip4p, shake 1e-10, 50 steps; the fdotr lj/cut sub-style and the explicit TIP4P virial are summed by the hybrid
# Earlier measured max relative error (before tightening), engine vs native (thermo rows of steps 0-50, final atoms; the atom v and f errors use a floor of 1e-3): pe 6.3e-8, evdwl 2.5e-8, ecoul 2.5e-9, press 1.3e-7; x 1.5e-8, v 2.5e-6, f 7.9e-6. The pure lj/cut/tip4p/long case w12tip4p_long gives pe 1.6e-8 and press 1.3e-7 on the same water, so the 1e-8 level is not reached by any TIP4P case here (SHAKE trajectory and PPPM sums). Sources: src/pair_hybrid.cpp at b332f28 (PairHybrid::compute), src/KSPACE/pair_lj_cut_tip4p_long.cpp.
units           real
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
read_data       w12tip4p_long_water.data
pair_style      hybrid/overlay lj/cut/tip4p/long 1 2 1 1 0.1546 8.5 lj/cut 8.5
pair_coeff      1 1 lj/cut/tip4p/long 0.1852 3.1589
pair_coeff      1 2 lj/cut/tip4p/long 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 lj/cut/tip4p/long 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 lj/cut 0.1 2.0
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 450.0 0.9572
angle_style     harmonic
angle_coeff     1 55.0 104.52
kspace_style    pppm/tip4p 1.0e-5
kspace_modify   gewald 0.37833912 mesh 12 12 12 order 5
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        1.0
fix             1 all shake 1.0e-10 200 0 b 1 a 1
fix             2 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl ecoul elong press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             50
